4. THE CLASS BOUND (INFERRED)
   for n like FETs G (by Ciss) and T together need Ciss(max) x R under 5 nF x 4 (n - 1) B / (bar I^2 n), rising with n to 52.87 nF.mOhm for a 175 C part (limit 150 C) and 31.45 for a 150 C part (limit 125 C); by QG the same limit is 528.7 nC.mOhm and 314.5
   every part read with a printed Ciss maximum sits above its limit (the lowest, BSC060P03NS3E G, 36.1 nF.mOhm on its screen bound, against its own limit); the parts with no printed maximum give no G at any count; so no set of the parts read meets G and T together at ANY count, whatever the count's pour

